    "https://albany.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205572": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Accreditation & Strategic Planning - Dean's Office-School of Business",
      "description": "University at Albany\nJob Posting: Associate Director of Accreditation & Strategic Planning - Dean's Office-School of Business University at Albany \n\tJob Posting: Associate Director of Accreditation & Strategic Planning - Dean's Office-School of Business Title Home About Employment Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Associate Director of Accreditation & Strategic Planning - Dean's Office-School of Business Category: Promotional Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Dean's Office--School of Business - 02201 Locations: Albany, NY Posted: Oct 7, 2026 Closes: Oct 21, 2026 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: Full-time Ref. No.: WF260127p Position ID: 205572 Share About University at Albany: The University at Albany is a Carnegie-classified Research 1 institution driven by academic excellence, pioneering research and scientific discovery, and service to community. UAlbany's world-class faculty experts and approximately 17,500 students are creating new knowledge in fields such as artificial intelligence, semiconductor engineering, atmospheric and environmental sciences, cybersecurity, public health, public administration and social welfare while deepening our understanding of our world through scholarship and creative activity in the social sciences and humanities. As one of the most diverse public research institutions in the nation, the University is a national leader in public engagement, educational equity and social mobility. For over 180 years, UAlbany has molded bright, curious and engaged students and launched them toward success. Located in Albany, New York, New York State's capital, the University is convenient to Boston, New York City, and the Adirondacks. Job Description: The Massry School of Business at the University at Albany is an AACSB-accredited school dedicated to excellence in teaching, research, student success, and community engagement. To support its accreditation, assessment, and strategic planning goals, the School seeks an Associate Director of Accreditation & Strategic Planning to coordinate accreditation activities, manage assurance of learning processes, and provide data-driven support for continuous improvement and strategic decision-making. The Associate Director of Accreditation & Strategic Planning is responsible for coordinating accreditation activities, managing assurance of learning processes, and supporting strategic planning initiatives that advance the School's academic quality and continuous improvement goals. Working closely with the Associate Dean for Academic Affairs, faculty, department chairs, and university partners, the position oversees the collection, analysis, and reporting of data required for accreditation compliance, assessment, rankings, and strategic decision-making. The Associate Director develops reporting tools and dashboards, monitors key performance indicators, and helps ensure that institutional priorities, accreditation standards, and continuous improvement efforts are effectively integrated across the School. Primary Responsibilities: Lead and coordinate AACSB accreditation activities , including annual reporting, accreditation record maintenance, preparation of self-study materials, support for peer review visits, and monitoring compliance with AACSB standards. Collect, analyze, and report accreditation-related data supporting AACSB requirements in areas such as strategic management, learner success, societal impact, thought leadership, assurance of learning, faculty qualifications, and teaching effectiveness. Manage faculty qualification processes , including administering qualification surveys, collecting and maintaining faculty curricula vitae, analyzing qualification data, and preparing related accreditation reports. Coordinate assurance of learning (AoL) initiatives by maintaining assessment plans and calendars, communicating assessment requirements, monitoring assessment completion, and supporting faculty in implementing direct and indirect assessment measures. Compile, analyze, and disseminate assessment results , preparing annual AoL reports, dashboards, and other materials that inform curricular review and continuous improvement efforts Monitor and document continuous improvement actions (\"closing the loop\") , tracking resulting curricular, pedagogical, and programmatic changes and maintaining evidence for accreditation review. Support strategic planning initiatives by collecting, tracking, and analyzing key performance indicators related to research productivity, student success, enrollment, career outcomes, fundraising, and program development. Develop reports, dashboards, and data visualizations that support evidence-based decision-making by School leadership, faculty governance bodies, advisory boards, and other stakeholders. Coordinate external reporting and benchmarking activities , including submissions for national and international rankings and participation in relevant accreditation and professional development workshops, conferences, and webinars. Foster collaboration across the School and University , serving as a liaison with academic departments, administrative units, and the Office of Institutional Research to support accreditation, assessment, strategic planning, and continuous improvement initiatives. Other reasonable duties as assigned Functional and Supervisory Relationships: Reports to: Associate Dean of Academic Affairs Supervises the following positions: None Job Requirements: Ability to work independently while managing multiple projects and deadlines in a fast-paced academic environment. Ability to build collaborative relationships with faculty, department chairs, administrators, and external accreditation representatives. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects, coordinate competing priorities, and meet established deadlines. Strong written, verbal, organizational, and interpersonal communication skills. Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel, and data reporting or dashboard tools. Applicants must demonstrate an ability to develop inclusive and equitable relationships within our diverse campus community. Applicants must demonstrate an ability to support diversity, equity, access, inclusion, and belonging relative to their role. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree from a college or University accredited by the US Department of Education or internationally recognized accrediting organization. 5 to 7 years of relevant experience in higher education, accreditation, institutional effectiveness, assessment, strategic planning, institutional research, or a related area. Experience collecting, analyzing, and presenting data to support organizational decision-making and reporting requirements. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree from a college or University accredited by the US Department of Education or internationally recognized accrediting organization. Experience supporting AACSB accreditation or other specialized/programmatic accreditation processes. Experience with assurance of learning, outcomes assessment, curriculum assessment, or institutional effectiveness initiatives in higher education. Experience developing dashboards, reports, and data visualizations using tools such as Power BI, Tableau, or similar platforms. Experience working collaboratively with faculty, academic leadership, and external stakeholders in a shared governance environment. Working Environment: Typical office environment Additional Information: This is a promotional opportunity for current UAlbany employees. Eligibility for Consideration: You must be employed at the University at Albany campus. You must be in a State-funded UUP professional position (MC employees are not eligible). You must have a permanent, term, or probationary appointment. Only temporary employees employed by UAlbany for three or more consecutive years can be considered eligible. For details concerning the University's Promotion Policy for Professional Employees, please see HR Memorandum 88-4 . Professional Rank and Salary Grade: Staff Associate, SL4, $75,000-80,000 Special Note: Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. If you currently need sponsorship or will need it in the future to maintain employment authorization, you do not meet eligibility requirements. Additionally, please note that UAlbany is not an E-Verify employer. The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, without exception, prepare, publish and distribute an Annual Security Report. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University's crime statistics for the past three years; and disclosures regarding the University's current campus security policies. The University at Albany's Annual Security Report is available in portable document format [PDF] by clicking this link http://police.albany.edu/ASR.shtml Pursuant to New York Labor Law §194-a, the University will not seek, request, or rely upon an applicant's wage or salary history in determining whether to interview, hire, or establish compensation for an applicant. Applicants are not required to provide wage or salary history information as a condition of employment consideration. Salary history may only be verified in the limited circumstances permitted by law. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process, including interviews, please contact Rhonda Haines, the University's Designee for Reasonable Accommodations (DRA) in the Office of Human Resources, at rlhaines@albany.edu or (518) 437-4700; requests for accommodation will be considered in accordance with applicable law. THE UNIVERSITY AT ALBANY IS AN EO/AA/IRCA/ADA EMPLOYER Please apply online via http://albany.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=205572 Application Instructions: Applicants MUST submit the following documents: Resume Cover letter stating all the required minimum qualifications and any of the applicable preferred qualifications List of 3 professional references with e-mail addresses and telephone numbers Note : After submitting your resume, the subsequent pages give you instructions for uploading additional documents (i.e. cover letter etc.). See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your UAlbany Careers Account to check your completed application. Closing date for receipt of applications: October 21. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation University at Albany, State University of New York 1400 Washington Ave Albany, NY 12222"
    },
    "https://albany.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205539": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Associate or Visiting Assistant Professor - Cybersecurity",
      "description": "University at Albany\nJob Posting: Postdoctoral Associate or Visiting Assistant Professor - Cybersecurity University at Albany \n\tJob Posting: Postdoctoral Associate or Visiting Assistant Professor - Cybersecurity Title Home About Employment Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Postdoctoral Associate or Visiting Assistant Professor - Cybersecurity Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Cybersecurity - 04042 Locations: Albany, NY Posted: Oct 6, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: WF260164 Position ID: 205539 Share About University at Albany: The University at Albany is a Carnegie-classified Research 1 institution driven by academic excellence, pioneering research and scientific discovery, and service to community. UAlbany's world-class faculty experts and approximately 17,500 students are creating new knowledge in fields such as artificial intelligence, semiconductor engineering, atmospheric and environmental sciences, cybersecurity, public health, public administration and social welfare while deepening our understanding of our world through scholarship and creative activity in the social sciences and humanities. As one of the most diverse public research institutions in the nation, the University is a national leader in public engagement, educational equity and social mobility. For over 180 years, UAlbany has molded bright, curious and engaged students and launched them toward success. Located in Albany, New York, New York State's capital, the University is convenient to Boston, New York City and the Adirondacks. Job Description: About CEHC : The mission of the College of Emergency Preparedness, Homeland Security, and Cybersecurity (CEHC) is to bring together people, technology and knowledge to address the challenges of the 21st century. We accomplish this through high-quality academic programs, an interdisciplinary and entrepreneurial spirit, enthusiasm for learning and teaching, the operational application of knowledge, and cutting-edge research initiatives. CEHC is committed to ensuring that our learning, living, and working environments demonstrate respect for all and are free from inequality and discrimination. More about CEHC at https://www.albany.edu/cehc About the Cybersecurity Department : Our society is interconnected and increasingly dependent on our cyber-systems. From personal and business communications to smarter, greener energy grids, our reliance on the computer networks binding us all together grows daily. Securing these vital connections becomes ever more challenging. The Cybersecurity Department's goal is to help our students learn to face that challenge and to help provide digital protections to people and society in general. We offer minor, major, and MS programs in Cybersecurity, and are part of the University's interdisciplinary Information Science Ph.D. program, through its concentration in Information Assurance. Our programs prepare students for innovative cybersecurity careers protecting data, devices, computers and networks from a wide range of threats. The fast-growing and dynamic Cybersecurity Department boasts a talented faculty with expertise across the various areas of cybersecurity. In addition, the Department shares CEHC and the University's goals of an engaging and student-focused program that both keeps pace with changes in cybersecurity and prepares students for the wide array of future experience that await them in the field. UAlbany cybersecurity students are part of a community that is dedicated to preparing them to participate in the increasingly necessary roles protecting people and their digital assets in the modern world. More about the Cybersecurity Department at www.albany.edu/cehc/departments/cybersecurity. The Cybersecurity Department of CEHC at the University at Albany, State University of New York, is seeking applicants for a Promoting Recruitment, Opportunity, Diversity, Inclusion and Growth Plus ( PRODIG+ ) Fellowship within the Cybersecurity Department. The PRODiG+ Fellowship is designed with two primary goals: (1) increase the number and share of excellent and diverse faculty committed to advancing the ideals of diversity, equity, and inclusion; and (2) strengthen the pathway for retention and support of these candidates. The Postdoctoral fellow will work with one or more faculty members on their ongoing research. This position will include expectations for research, writing, and publishing results in high-impact venues. The position title will be Visiting Assistant Professor or Postdoctoral Associate depending on the background and experience of the candidate. This is a 12-month position that is expected to be two years in duration and may lead to a potential appointment of a tenure track faculty position. Additional information on the PRODIG+ Fellowship can be found at https://www.suny.edu/prodig-plus/fellowship/ . The PRODiG+ Fellowship is open to any and all prospective candidates regardless of race, color, national origin, or sex, and is consistent with all current governing federal and state nondiscrimination law. All application submissions will be assessed and evaluated in accordance with the required eligibility criteria. Although the areas of specialization within the broader field of cybersecurity are open, preference will be given to candidates whose research program investigates the socio-technical, institutional, and human dimensions of cybersecurity. Areas of particular interest include, but are not limited to: Cybersecurity policy, international cyber practices, and internet governance Cyber law, regulatory compliance, and digital liability Usable security, human behavior, and organizational risk culture The economics of cybersecurity and cyber insurance Information integrity, digital platform policy, and surveillance ethics While candidates must demonstrate a deep understanding of core cybersecurity concepts, priority will be given to scholars whose primary methodologies draw from the social sciences, public policy, law, human-computer interaction, or information science, rather than traditional low-level systems or network engineering. Candidates whose research areas intersect with scholars in CEHC and the wider University are also preferred. The Fellow will work closely with other faculty to advance their personal research portfolio with peer-reviewed publications, presentations at national/international conferences, and grant proposal development. The Visiting Assistant Professor or Postdoctoral Associate will be mentored by experienced faculty and will have access to campus resources for both research and teaching skill development. Primary Responsibilities: Advancing and promoting cybersecurity research independently, and in collaboration with Cybersecurity faculty. Developing their teaching in selected undergraduate and/or graduate courses in cybersecurity. Mentoring undergraduate and/or graduate students in research. Dissertation committee participation. Potential supervision of doctoral research. Selected service to the department and college. Job Requirements: Fellows are welcome to focus on a wide range of scholarly topics and disciplinary areas with an emphasis on promoting and impacting DEI through scholarship, teaching, and service to the campus community. Applicants must demonstrate an ability to develop inclusive and equitable relationships within our diverse campus community. Applicants must demonstrate an ability to support diversity, equity, access, inclusion, and belonging relative to their role. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants are expected to possess a Doctorate in Cybersecurity by August 21, 2027, or a related field prior to the start of the appointment, from an accredited college or University. Be eligible to work in the United States without a visa sponsorship. (Note: if you currently need sponsorship or will need it in the future to maintain employment authorization, you do not meet the eligibility requirements for this position) Demonstrate an academic/scholarly track record relevant to cybersecurity. Demonstrate personal, academic, and/or work experience engaging with Diversity, Equity and Inclusion and/or a commitment to facilitating and enhancing DEI efforts in the campus community. Such experience may include, but is not limited to, an academic/scholarly track record focused on DEI; work, volunteer/unpaid/community service; or related experience/expertise in serving underserved or vulnerable areas and/or populations Preferred Qualifications: A clear plan for developing a scholarly agenda in cybersecurity at UAlbany Participation in, applying for, or obtaining extramural research funding. Demonstrate breadth of interest, capability, and collegial relationship maturity across a wide range of areas relevant to cybersecurity research and teaching. Demonstrated experience with related disciplines, collaboration principles, and the operation of various sub-areas of cybersecurity. This includes understanding the ethical underpinnings, necessary protections, data sources, privacy, and areas of critical economic or societal importance. Ability to develop classes in existing and emerging subfields of cybersecurity, especially those aligned with the research they are engaging in at UAlbany. Preference will be given to candidates who are: Current SUNY students, alumni, and/or Fellows. From a low-income background (e.g., Pell-eligible as undergraduates), were first- generation college students (students whose parents have not earned a bachelor's degree), have overcome adversity, are AmeriCorps alumni, or are veterans. Working Environment: Typical office environment Additional Information: Professional Rank and Salary Range: Postdoctoral Associate, Salary commensurate with experience. The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, without exception, prepare, publish and distribute an Annual Security Report. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University's crime statistics for the past three years; and disclosures regarding the University's current campus security policies. The University at Albany's Annual Security Report is available in portable document format [PDF] by clicking this link http://police.albany.edu/ASR.shtml Pursuant to New York Labor Law §194-a, the University will not seek, request, or rely upon an applicant's wage or salary history in determining whether to interview, hire, or establish compensation for an applicant. Applicants are not required to provide wage or salary history information as a condition of employment consideration. Salary history may only be verified in the limited circumstances permitted by law. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process, including interviews, please contact Rhonda Haines, the University's Designee for Reasonable Accommodations (DRA) in the Office of Human Resources, at rlhaines@albany.edu or (518) 437-4700; requests for accommodation will be considered in accordance with applicable law. THE UNIVERSITY AT ALBANY IS AN EO/AA/IRCA/ADA EMPLOYER Please apply online via http://albany.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=205539 Application Instructions: Applicants MUST submit the following documents: CV Cover letter stating all the required minimum qualifications and any of the applicable preferred qualifications. Statements of research and teaching interests and experience Applicants must also submit a short essay (750 words or less) in response to the prompt: \"Please describe how you've engaged, facilitated, and/or enhanced diversity, equity, and inclusion efforts in the campus community. Examples could include personal, academic, and/or work experience and may include, but is not limited to, an academic/scholarly track record focused on diversity, equity, and inclusion; work, volunteer/unpaid/ community service; or related experience/expertise in serving underserved or vulnerable areas and/or populations.\" Contact information for three references See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your UAlbany Careers Account to check your completed application. Preference will be given to applications received by November 4. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation University at Albany, State University of New York 1400 Washington Ave Albany, NY 12222"
    },
    "https://albany.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205503": {
      "title": "Plant Utilities Engineer 1 (NY HELPS) (Power Plant)",
      "description": "University at Albany\nJob Posting: Plant Utilities Engineer 1 (NY HELPS) (Power Plant) University at Albany \n\tJob Posting: Plant Utilities Engineer 1 (NY HELPS) (Power Plant) Title Home About Employment Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Plant Utilities Engineer 1 (NY HELPS) (Power Plant) Category: Civil Service Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Power Plant - 03068 Locations: Albany, NY Posted: Oct 5, 2026 Closes: Oct 21, 2026 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: Full-time Ref. No.: WF260145, Line 01405 Salary Type: Annually Position ID: 205503 Share About University at Albany: The University at Albany is a Carnegie-classified Research 1 institution driven by academic excellence, pioneering research and scientific discovery, and service to community.  UAlbany's world-class faculty experts and approximately 17,500 students are creating new knowledge in fields such as artificial intelligence, semiconductor engineering, atmospheric and environmental sciences, cybersecurity, public health, public administration and social welfare while deepening our understanding of our world through scholarship and creative activity in the social sciences and humanities.  As one of the most diverse public research institutions in the nation, the University is a national leader in public engagement, educational equity and social mobility.  For over 180 years, UAlbany has molded bright, curious and engaged students and launched them toward success. Located in Albany, New York, New York State's capital, the University is convenient to Boston, New York City, and the Adirondacks Job Description: Vacancy #: WF260145 Apply by: October 21, 2026 Title: Plant Utilities Engineer 1 (NY HELPS) Location: Power Plant Salary: $59,049 Grade: SG-14 (CSEA) Hours: Saturday thru Wednesday 3:00 PM to 11:00 PM (pass days Thursday/Friday) Duration: Contingent Permanent Requirements: This title is part of the New York Hiring for Emergency Limited Placement Statewide Program ( NY HELPS ). For the duration of the NY HELPS Program, this title maybe filled via a non-competitive appointment, which means no examination is required but all candidates must meet the minimum qualifications of the title for which they apply.  At a future date (within one year of permanent appointment), it is expected employees hired under NY HELPS will have their non-competitive employment status converted to competitive status, without having to compete in an examination. Employees will then be afforded with all of the same rights and privileges of competitive class employees of New York State. While serving permanently in a NY HELPS title, employees may take part in any promotion examination for which they are qualified. NON-COMPETITIVE MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS (NY HELPS): Either 1 . Graduate of heating, HVAC, ventilation, air conditioning, and refrigeration apprenticeship program from the U.S. Air Force; Or 2. Must have been an enlisted machinery technician (MK) with the U.S. Coast Guard OR possession of a certificate as a Marine Engineer issued by the U.S. Coast Guard; Or 3. Must have been an enlisted power generation equipment repairer with the U.S. Army; Or 4. Must have been an enlisted gas turbine systems technician, submarine nuclear propulsion plant operator reactor control, utilities man, machinist mate, or engineman with the U.S. Navy; Or 5. Must have a Merchant Mariner's Document (MMD) and have been a qualified member of the engine department (QMED) as an oiler, fireman/water tender, refrigerating engineer or engineman with the U.S. Merchant Marine; Or 6. Completion of a New York State Department of Labor registered apprenticeship program for stationary engineers, plant maintenance (plumber/steamfitter), HVAC Mechanic or plant maintenance (refrigeration/AC) (See Note #1); Or 7. Possession of a High-Pressure Boiler Operating Engineer License or Stationary Engineer License; Or 8. A bachelor's degree in Facilities Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or Marine Engineering; Or 9. Four years of full-time hands on experience in the maintenance and operation of commercial, industrial, institutional facility, computer applications of digital energy platforms and building analytics and/or performing diagnosis, repair of HVAC systems or boilers or auxiliary equipment; Or 10. Four years of full-time hands on experience in a residential setting performing diagnosis, operation, maintenance repair of HVAC systems or boilers or auxiliary equipment; Or 11. An associate's degree in HVAC AND two years of qualifying experience as described in EITHER qualification #9 or #10 above; Or 12. Completion of an HVAC certificate or diploma from a BOCES program ( 900 hours ) OR completion of an approved certificate in HVAC, electrical, refrigeration, boiler operations and maintenance, or plumbing from an accredited technical school or technology college (See Note #2) AND two years of qualifying experience as described in EITHER qualification #9 or #10 above. Note #1  Information regarding qualifying New York State Department of Labor recognized apprenticeship programs can be found here: https://labor.ny.gov/apprenticeship/appindex.shtm [(External Link)] . Note # 2  Certification programs must be accredited by the Accrediting Commission of Career Schools and Colleges (ACCSC) or recognized by the New York State Education Department Bureau of Proprietary School Supervision (BPSS). Information on ACCSC accredited programs can be found here: http://www.accsc.org/ [(External Link)] . Information on BPSS recognized proprietary schools can be found here: http://www.acces.nysed.gov/bpss/welcome-career-training-proprietary-schools [(External Link)] . COMPETITIVE MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS (NON-NY HELPS): Candidates must have a reachable score on the University at Albany Plant Utilities Engineer 1 Exam List OR Be a current NYS employee and have a current permanent appointment with 1 year of service as a Plant Utilities Engineer 1, or in a title eligible to transfer to Plant Utilities Engineer 1 OR Be a former NYS employee eligible for reinstatement to the title of Plant Utilities Engineer 1 May be filled from a mandatory reemployment list if one is in effect at the time of appointment. Any applications received that do not meet the above requirements as described will be deemed unqualified. Additional Information: Special Notes: Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. If you currently need sponsorship or will need it in the future to maintain employment authorization, you do not meet eligibility requirements. Additionally, please note that UAlbany is not an E-Verify employer. The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, without exception, prepare, publish, and distribute an Annual Security Report. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University's crime statistics for the past three years; and disclosures regarding the University's current campus security policies. The University at Albany's Annual Security Report is available in portable document format [PDF] by clicking this link http://police.albany.edu/ASR.shtml Pursuant to New York Labor Law §194-a, the University will not seek, request, or rely upon an applicant's wage or salary history in determining whether to interview, hire, or establish compensation for an applicant. Applicants are not required to provide wage or salary history information as a condition of employment consideration. Salary history may only be verified in the limited circumstances permitted by law. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process, including interviews, please contact Rhonda Haines, the University's Designee for Reasonable Accommodations (DRA) in the Office of Human Resources, at rlhaines@albany.edu or (518) 437-4700; requests for accommodation will be considered in accordance with applicable law. THE UNIVERSITY AT ALBANY IS AN EO/AA/IRCA/ADA EMPLOYER Application Instructions: Applicants must submit the below documents through the online application process.  Accommodations can be provided to applicants who need assistance applying online . Classified Employment Application Form Employment and Experience Form Optional : Resume and/or cover letter may be uploaded as an additional document. Please note that the application and employment forms must still be completed in their entirety. Note: The required forms are included in the online application process, which will be found after clicking \"apply now\" See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your UAlbany Careers Account to check your completed application. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation University at Albany, State University of New York 1400 Washington Ave Albany, NY 12222"
    },
