    "https://albany.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205459": {
      "title": "Nurse Practitioner/Physician Assistant - Student Health Services",
      "description": "University at Albany\nJob Posting: Nurse Practitioner/Physician Assistant - Student Health Services University at Albany \n\tJob Posting: Nurse Practitioner/Physician Assistant - Student Health Services Title Home About Employment Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Nurse Practitioner/Physician Assistant - Student Health Services Category: Professional Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Student Health Services - 05007 Locations: Albany, NY Posted: Oct 2, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: WF260109 Position ID: 205459 Share About University at Albany: The University at Albany is a Carnegie-classified Research 1 institution driven by academic excellence, pioneering research and scientific discovery, and service to community. UAlbany's world-class faculty experts and approximately 17,500 students are creating new knowledge in fields such as artificial intelligence, semiconductor engineering, atmospheric and environmental sciences, cybersecurity, public health, public administration and social welfare while deepening our understanding of our world through scholarship and creative activity in the social sciences and humanities. As one of the most diverse public research institutions in the nation, the University is a national leader in public engagement, educational equity and social mobility. For over 180 years, UAlbany has molded bright, curious and engaged students and launched them toward success. Located in Albany, New York, New York State's capital, the University is convenient to Boston, New York City, and the Adirondacks. Job Description: Student Health Services at UAlbany sits within the Division of Student Affairs & Enrollment and provides compassionate and inclusive healthcare to all registered UAlbany students. The Advanced Practice Provider (Nurse Practitioner or Physician Assistant) will provide quality medical and gynecological services to a diverse student population as part of an outpatient clinic and will participate in health education and community outreach activities related to the University Student Health Services. This is a unique opportunity to practice in a dynamic university health setting that prioritizes quality, access, and whole-person care over high-volume, throughput-driven models. This role is ideal for a clinician who enjoys working with emerging adults and is motivated to contribute to both patient care and the systems that support it. Primary Responsibilities: Manage medical and gynecological concerns, which includes: Assessment and diagnosis, providing patient health education, ordering laboratory tests, radiology tests and prescribing medications, including birth control. Manage and respond daily to EMR tasks from nursing and patients. Keep timely and meticulous health records Provide physicals for sports, study abroad and academic-related activities Evaluate MMR/TB status regarding administrative health requirement Refer to specialty or emergency care as appropriate Work with University Counseling and Psychological Services for referring and receiving referrals Liaison with Albany County Department of Health for reporting and management of certain communicable diseases Work inter-departmentally with other UAlbany departments on an as needed basis. Participate in orientation and other outreach for students Provide health screening and education and assist in the development and implementation of preventive healthcare Other reasonable duties as assigned Functional and Supervisory Relationships: Reports to Medical Director or Designated Physician May supervise employees as assigned (if no direct reports at time of filling position) Job Requirements: Knowledge of Electronic Medical Records and electronic N.Y.S. prescription prescribing procedures. Demonstrated skill in providing effective care to diverse range of personal and cultural backgrounds. Ability to conduct efficient and effective triage and provide recommendations for medical care as well as referrals for other related services. Leadership and organizational skills, including the ability to provide leadership, oversight, and direction to assure Student Health Center goals, activities, and practices are consistent with and contribute to the department and University's goals and strategies. Ability to collaborate effectively with a multi-disciplinary team. Commitment to cultural humility and ongoing development of multicultural competency in the context of providing inclusive and equitable services. Applicants must demonstrate an ability to develop inclusive and equitable relationships within our diverse campus community. Applicants must demonstrate an ability to support diversity, equity, access, inclusion, and belonging relative to their role. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Nurse Practitioner or Physician Assistant degree from a college or University accredited by the US Department of Education or internationally recognized accrediting organization. Active Nurse Practitioner or Physician Assistant license to practice in New York State Current Board Certification as FNP or ANP or PA-C. Two years of post-graduate office-based primary care and/or urgent care experience Experience providing office-based primary medical and gynecologic care, including diagnosis and evidence-based evaluation and treatment. Experience providing medical care to a diverse adolescent/young adult population Preferred Qualifications: 1-2 years of experience working in Urgent Care settings. 1-2 years of experience working in College Health. 1-2 years of experience working with culturally diverse, adolescent, young adult population. Working Environment: Typical medical office environment Ability to be a professional resource for office staff from front desk, to nursing to lab staff Ability to provide both in person and telehealth medical care Ability to work with technology, including EMR and emails Additional Information: Professional Rank and Salary Grade: College Physician's Assistant, SL3, $90,000-95,000. Special Note: Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. If you currently need sponsorship or will need it in the future to maintain employment authorization, you do not meet eligibility requirements. Additionally, please note that UAlbany is not an E-Verify employer. The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, without exception, prepare, publish and distribute an Annual Security Report. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University's crime statistics for the past three years; and disclosures regarding the University's current campus security policies. The University at Albany's Annual Security Report is available in portable document format [PDF] by clicking this link http://police.albany.edu/ASR.shtml Pursuant to New York Labor Law §194-a, the University will not seek, request, or rely upon an applicant's wage or salary history in determining whether to interview, hire, or establish compensation for an applicant. Applicants are not required to provide wage or salary history information as a condition of employment consideration. Salary history may only be verified in the limited circumstances permitted by law. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process, including interviews, please contact Rhonda Haines, the University's Designee for Reasonable Accommodations (DRA) in the Office of Human Resources, at rlhaines@albany.edu or (518) 437-4700; requests for accommodation will be considered in accordance with applicable law. THE UNIVERSITY AT ALBANY IS AN EO/AA/IRCA/ADA EMPLOYER Please apply online via http://albany.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=205459 Application Instructions: Applicants MUST submit the following documents: Resume Cover letter stating all the required minimum qualifications and any of the applicable preferred qualifications List of 3 professional references with e-mail addresses and telephone numbers Note : After submitting your resume, the subsequent pages give you instructions for uploading additional documents (i.e. cover letter etc.). See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your UAlbany Careers Account to check your completed application. Preference will be given to applications received by October 16. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation University at Albany, State University of New York 1400 Washington Ave Albany, NY 12222"
