    "https://albany.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205142": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Chemistry",
      "description": "University at Albany\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor - Chemistry University at Albany \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor - Chemistry Title Home About Employment Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor - Chemistry Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Chemistry - 02107 Locations: Albany, NY Posted: Sep 24, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: WF260125 Position ID: 205142 Share About University at Albany: The University at Albany is a Carnegie-classified Research 1 institution driven by academic excellence, pioneering research and scientific discovery, and service to community. UAlbany's world-class faculty experts and approximately 17,500 students are creating new knowledge in fields such as artificial intelligence, semiconductor engineering, atmospheric and environmental sciences, cybersecurity, public health, public administration and social welfare while deepening our understanding of our world through scholarship and creative activity in the social sciences and humanities. As one of the most diverse public research institutions in the nation, the University is a national leader in public engagement, educational equity and social mobility. For over 180 years, UAlbany has molded bright, curious and engaged students and launched them toward success. Located in Albany, New York, New York State's capital, the University is convenient to Boston, New York City and the Adirondacks. Job Description: The Department of Chemistry within the College of Arts and Sciences at the University at Albany invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor (academic year).  The candidate will be an experimental chemist whose research addresses advanced materials design and engineering, semiconductor-related chemistry, sustainable/green chemistry, or other areas of applied chemical science. They will establish an externally funded research program and contribute to undergraduate and graduate education, with a particular emphasis on hands-on undergraduate research, workforce preparation, and industrial collaboration. This position will enable the department to launch an applied MS program in \"Industry Chemistry\" designed to attract current and future employees from regional industry partners. In addition to teaching Chemistry courses and courses in their area of expertise, the candidate will lead departmental efforts to incorporate green and sustainable chemistry principles across the Chemistry curriculum and laboratory programs, particularly to help \"greenify\" our gen-chem for nursing students, to reduce student exposure to hazardous substances and increase student success. The Department of Chemistry offers undergraduate and graduate programs that provide students with a strong foundation in the chemical sciences and opportunities for advanced research. The department's faculty pursue research across a broad range of areas in chemistry and related fields, fostering an interdisciplinary and collaborative research environment. Additionally, the Department of Chemistry and the College of Arts and Sciences offer a collaborative and supportive environment for faculty and students. This position emphasizes candidates who pursue excellence in research, demonstrate a commitment to teaching undergraduate and graduate courses, and contribute to the department's mission of fostering student success and scientific discovery. Primary Responsibilities: Research : Conduct innovative research in chemistry or a related field, publish findings in peer-reviewed journals, present research at professional meetings and conferences, mentor student researchers, and seek external funding to support a productive research program. Teaching : Teach and develop undergraduate and graduate chemistry courses, prepare course materials, mentor students, and foster their intellectual and professional development. Service : Contribute to the governance and functioning of the University, College, and Department through departmental and university service, student advising and mentoring, participation in admissions, and other professional and academic service activities. Functional and Supervisory Relationships: Reports to: Chair, Department of Chemistry Supervises: Graduate and undergraduate students, as well as laboratory personnel, including postdoctoral researchers, research scientists, technicians, and other research staff. Job Requirements: Applicants must demonstrate an ability to develop inclusive and equitable relationships within our diverse campus community. Applicants must demonstrate an ability to support diversity, equity, access, inclusion, and belonging relative to their role. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. degree in Chemistry or a closely related field from a college or university accredited by the U.S. Department of Education or an internationally recognized accrediting organization by 8/21/2027. A demonstrated potential for research in the field of Applied Chemistry. Potential to obtain independent extramural funding. Evidence of academic preparation, disciplinary expertise, and interest in teaching Chemistry. Preferred Qualifications: Completed postdoctoral research in Chemistry or a related field. Strong and growing record of impactful research and peer-reviewed publications. Demonstrated ability to secure external research funding. Experience teaching of undergraduate and/or graduate courses in various modalities. Experience mentoring undergraduate and/or graduate students in chemical research. Working Environment: Typical office and classroom environments. Experimental chemistry laboratory environments. Additional Information: Professional Rank and Salary Range: Assistant Professor (Academic-year appointment), Salary commensurate with experience. The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, without exception, prepare, publish and distribute an Annual Security Report. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University's crime statistics for the past three years; and disclosures regarding the University's current campus security policies. The University at Albany's Annual Security Report is available in portable document format [PDF] by clicking this link http://police.albany.edu/ASR.shtml Pursuant to New York Labor Law §194-a, the University will not seek, request, or rely upon an applicant's wage or salary history in determining whether to interview, hire, or establish compensation for an applicant. Applicants are not required to provide wage or salary history information as a condition of employment consideration. Salary history may only be verified in the limited circumstances permitted by law. THE UNIVERSITY AT ALBANY IS AN EO/AA/IRCA/ADA EMPLOYER Please apply online via http://albany.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=205142 Application Instructions: Applicants MUST submit the following documents: CV Cover letter stating all the required minimum qualifications and any of the applicable preferred qualifications. Research statement Teaching statement Contact information for three professional references See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your UAlbany Careers Account to check your completed application. Preference will be given to applications received by October 23. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation University at Albany, State University of New York 1400 Washington Ave Albany, NY 12222"
    },
    "https://albany.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205080": {
      "title": "Program Coordinator - Center for International Education & Global Strategy",
      "description": "University at Albany\nJob Posting: Program Coordinator - Center for International Education & Global Strategy University at Albany \n\tJob Posting: Program Coordinator - Center for International Education & Global Strategy Title Home About Employment Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Program Coordinator - Center for International Education & Global Strategy Category: Professional Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Center for International Education & Global Strategy - 02011 Locations: Albany, NY Posted: Sep 23, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: WF260105 Position ID: 205080 Share About University at Albany: The University at Albany is a Carnegie-classified Research 1 institution driven by academic excellence, pioneering research and scientific discovery, and service to community. UAlbany's world-class faculty experts and approximately 17,500 students are creating new knowledge in fields such as artificial intelligence, semiconductor engineering, atmospheric and environmental sciences, cybersecurity, public health, public administration and social welfare while deepening our understanding of our world through scholarship and creative activity in the social sciences and humanities. As one of the most diverse public research institutions in the nation, the University is a national leader in public engagement, educational equity and social mobility. For over 180 years, UAlbany has molded bright, curious and engaged students and launched them toward success. Located in Albany, New York, New York State's capital, the University is convenient to Boston, New York City, and the Adirondacks. Job Description: The Center for International Education and Global Strategy at the University at Albany, State University of New York, seeks to hire a Program Coordinator for Education Abroad. The Education Abroad office aims to provide accessible and inclusive global learning programs, experiences, and curricula intended to equip students with the life-long knowledge, attitudes, and skills necessary to be responsive global citizens in an ever-changing world. Primary Responsibilities: Advisement of students on education abroad opportunities in various regions especially in Asia, with emphasis on increasing enrollment in education abroad programs through oversight of recruitment/marketing efforts, liaising with academic departments at UAlbany, and effective use of the Terra Dotta application system. Development, administration, and promotion of education abroad programs. Communication and administrative coordination with overseas partner universities. Participation in and assistance with University at Albany Education Abroad office functions, including virtual presentations, facilitation of education abroad orientation and re-entry programs, review of education abroad applications, and management of correspondence with students and parents in relation to programs. Development and maintenance of education abroad promotional materials and resources, including program webpages and flyers. Contribution to the media and marketing events of the Education Abroad office. Other reasonable duties as assigned. Functional and Supervisory Relationships: Reports to Director, Education Abroad Supervises the following positions: student assistants/volunteers Job Requirements: Strong interpersonal, public speaking, and organizational skills. Demonstrated fluency in written and spoken English and ability to contribute to written public relations efforts. Demonstrated ability as a team player and ability to work independently. Applicants must demonstrate an ability to develop inclusive and equitable relationships within our diverse campus community. Applicants must demonstrate an ability to support diversity, equity, access, inclusion, and belonging relative to their role. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree from a college or University accredited by the US Department of Education or internationally recognized accrediting organization. At least 2 years of relevant experience working with college or university students in the field of International Education. Experience living or studying abroad. Preferred Qualifications: Foreign language ability, preferably Korean or Japanese. Prior experience managing study abroad programs. Experience with study abroad data and application management systems, such as Terra Dotta. Working Environment: Typical office environment Requires ability to occasionally travel both inside and outside of the United States Additional Information: Professional Rank and Salary Grade: Senior Staff Assistant, SL3, $60,245. Special Note: Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. If you currently need sponsorship or will need it in the future to maintain employment authorization, you do not meet eligibility requirements. Additionally, please note that UAlbany is not an E-Verify employer. The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, without exception, prepare, publish and distribute an Annual Security Report. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University's crime statistics for the past three years; and disclosures regarding the University's current campus security policies. The University at Albany's Annual Security Report is available in portable document format [PDF] by clicking this link http://police.albany.edu/ASR.shtml Pursuant to New York Labor Law §194-a, the University will not seek, request, or rely upon an applicant's wage or salary history in determining whether to interview, hire, or establish compensation for an applicant. Applicants are not required to provide wage or salary history information as a condition of employment consideration. Salary history may only be verified in the limited circumstances permitted by law. THE UNIVERSITY AT ALBANY IS AN EO/AA/IRCA/ADA EMPLOYER Please apply online via http://albany.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=205080 Application Instructions: Applicants MUST submit the following documents: Resume Cover letter stating all the required minimum qualifications and any of the applicable preferred qualifications List of 3 professional references with e-mail addresses and telephone numbers Note : After submitting your resume, the subsequent pages give you instructions for uploading additional documents (i.e. cover letter etc.). See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your UAlbany Careers Account to check your completed application. Preference will be given to applications received by October 27. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation University at Albany, State University of New York 1400 Washington Ave Albany, NY 12222"
    }
  },
